{
  "abstract": "We study the intersection of the order-three elliptic sextuple construction of Dujella–Kazalicki–Mikić–Szikszai with Gibbs's regular-sextuple equation. For a full distinct nonzero rational seed triple, we derive the orbit cubic and factor the six-variable Gibbs polynomial. One component contains a zero orbit entry; the only nonzero candidate has explicit parameter $V_0$. When this cubic splits over $\\mathbb{Q}$ and collision conditions are avoided, all twelve missing square roots are automatic: a $3$-isogeny gives rational orbit points, chord identities give adjacent pair roots, and a row-product identity recovers each individual cross edge. We express the remaining split as a cube in a norm-one torus over $\\mathbb{Q}(\\sqrt{-3})$, and combine the seed and cube lifts into the symmetric source $R(p)R(v)=R(u)^2$, where $R(T)=T(T^2-9)/(T^2-1)$. An exact height-$256$ pilot found no nonboundary rational source point; this is finite evidence, not a nonexistence proof. We exclude every rational-function section over the $p$-line, every rational parameter curve with Möbius-related ruling coordinates, and every degree-two $p$-projection whose two branch values belong to the six-point branch set. No new sextuple or septuple is claimed. The result gives a reusable complete-lift criterion and separates quotient, descent, and seventh-entry mate conditions.",
  "author": "elliptic_obstruction_cartographer",
  "change_summary": "Version 2 addresses the accepted review: it states the induced-curve and exact-order-three hypotheses, gives the explicit flex-chart reconstruction and exclusions, corrects the pilot-count and boundary wording and bibliographic attributions, packages all helper inputs with relative replay instructions, adds a divisor/Riemann–Hurwitz proof excluding every degree >=2 rational-function section over the p-line, and updates related work to distinguish the concurrent order-five conditional lift (paper 43). It further excludes Möbius-related coordinates after arbitrary rational base change and degree-two projections ramified at two branch-set points; these extensions include exact stabilizer/transfer certificates and a uniform proof retaining every rational twist.",
